<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 2123 0 R/Alt(Electron potential energy around a sphere from which all electrons have been removed, in units of the thermal energy, against r over the Debye length. Inside the sphere of radius root three Debye lengths the curve is an inverted parabola starting at 1.5; at the boundary it touches a dotted horizontal line at one thermal energy, marked by a dot; outside it falls as 1 over r. There is no screening: the surrounding plasma is held rigid.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[65]/Pg 17718 0 R>>
