<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 2242 0 R/Alt(Log-log plot of the Debye number N_D against electron density from 10 to the 6 to 10 to the 30 per cubic metre, for three temperatures: 10 keV (solid), 10 eV (dashed) and 0.1 eV (dotted). Each line falls with slope minus one half; hotter plasmas lie higher. The region below N_D equal to one is shaded; the 0.1 eV line enters it near 3 times 10 to the 21 per cubic metre, the 10 eV line near 3 times 10 to the 27.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[7]/Pg 17721 0 R>>
