<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 2612 0 R/Alt(Two plots against k times the Debye length on a logarithmic axis from 0.01 to 100. Left: one over epsilon of k, the net charge over the imposed charge, rises from zero at long wavelengths through one half at k lambda_D equal to one to one at short wavelengths. Right: the Fourier-space potential of a point charge on logarithmic axes; the dashed bare Coulomb potential falls as one over k squared everywhere, while the solid screened potential is flat below k lambda_D of about one and joins the bare curve above it.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[0 1]/Pg 17726 0 R>>
